{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The streaked, etc. — akudim, nekudim, and berudim.</b> One needs to know what the meaning of berudim is; even if it be a type among those born in the flock, since Jacob has no share in it, for it was not mentioned in the conditions — if so, why did they show it to him in the dream?" "<b>And I saw</b> in the master, Rabbi ibn Ezra, who wrote that berudim are spotted, but the master did not bring a compelling proof for the matter. Further, according to what he said, ״אִם כֹּה יֹאמַר״ etc. (Genesis 31:8), it has been made known that Jacob would take only either akudim or nekudim — and from this, why were there coming up on the flock types that are not Jacob's portion?" "<b>Now</b> the reason for the matter is on account of what has preceded us concerning the knowledge of Laban the deceiver — for besides his schemes and his deceptions, he also had terafim that would tell him everything, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Tanchuma), and he would plainly inquire of them and know the fetuses in the full womb and their appearance. And from this, by virtue of this matter, Jacob's efforts were nullified for every type — however he might contrive, the terafim would cause him loss. Therefore He who answers in the time of distress answered him. And you should know that the type of appearance that will be in the offspring is formed at the time of mating, and there is no possibility of reversing it afterward except by means of a great miracle to reverse nature in a great reversal — and this thing is difficult in the eyes of El Elyon to do. Go out and learn from the words of our Sages of blessed memory in several places (Sotah 2a; Shabbat 23a), and HaShem made wisdom so as not to need to overturn the order of the nature of Creation — namely, that three types would come up together, and in each offspring, by the hylic power, all three were imprinted together. And by this the knowledge of the terafim was utterly nullified. And with the emergence of the offspring, the type that they agreed upon was revealed in them — that this is Jacob's portion. And let the matter not be far from your mind, for there are birds that change their colors to several appearances, and this is because HaShem imprinted this in them; likewise HaShem did with the offspring of Laban's flock, to deliver the oppressed from the hand of the oppressor. And His saying <b>berudim</b>, according to what we have explained, we find support for the words of Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra, that it is a spotted type — for otherwise, perhaps Laban would say, ״spotted shall be your wage,״ and the miracle would turn out to be for nothing, heaven forbid. Rather, surely berudim is a spotted type. And perhaps it is called so because its white is very white like hail (barad). And from this the verse is reconciled correctly." "<b>For I have seen et all that Laban does, etc.</b> The angel told him the reason for the miracle — that HaShem saw all his deeds and the cunning of Laban, and what he would contrive and inquire of his terafim, and there was no possibility of saving him from it except through the deed that He showed him coming up on the flock, as we have explained." "<b>Also</b> he hinted to him that all of Laban's doings are given over to Him, and therefore he did not say ״all that Laban does to you,״ to hint as well that all the offspring would be Jacob's portion — and there is no robbery in this, for HaShem is a righteous judge and knows all that he deceived and oppressed him, and He takes from this one and gives to that one, and He judges with righteousness."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {2 "The citation ״(סוטה ב., שבת כ״ג)״ refers to Sotah 2a and Shabbat 23a, standard Talmudic references."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:23.309017992Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}